<title>USA: Crossmann Communities backlog up.</title>
<headline>Crossmann Communities backlog up.</headline>
<dateline>INDIANAPOLIS 1997-02-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Crossmann Communities Inc said Monday that, as of December 31, it had a sales backlog of 1,006 homes with an aggregate sales value of about $108.1 million, up from 757 homes valued at $79.6 million a year ago.</p>
<p>Crossmann said it closed 711 new home sales in the fourth quarter of 1996, up from 551 in 1995.</p>
<p>Earlier, Crossmann reported fourth quarter earnings of $1.02 a share, up from $0.68 a year ago.</p>
<p>Crossmann builds single-family homes in Indiana, Ohio and Kentucky.</p>
<p>((Reuters Chicago Newsdesk (312) 408-8787))</p>
